# 026 - a numeric string outside i64 gives the SAME Value error as a
# non-numeric one (§6/.41 D): bad_int covers the whole failure family.
# Pair this with 008: identical message text, different VARIANT and stage - a
# literal too big never runs (Lex), int() of the same digits fails mid-run
# (Value), which is the distinction error.rs's doc comment insists on.
--- source
print int("9223372036854775808");
--- expect
error: Value at line 1: not a valid integer: 9223372036854775808
